There are a few times when you get a "call this scroll" prompt other
than as a result of reading it, so you may not have had a chance to
un-#name it.  The only examples that come to mind are when

1) a fleeing monster reads teleport, but fails to teleport (no-teleport
level or cursed-teleport to the same level) or

2) a hostile monster reads create monster, but no monster appears
(because it's in some way hidden from you)

Both of these are common enough scrolls that I'm likely to find and
identify them before long, so I think that #naming scrolls by price
isn't too great a loss.


